        "id": 1117279
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-20T21:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The radio on nRF51 can be used to implement multiple standards, but only one at a time.  I figured that that would be true of most chips that we\u0027d think of using.\n\nI was suprised that only some of these channels are protected with ifdefs, but I ran into the limit when I tried to add CC_RADIO without the ifdef for one of the boards (cr50?)",
      "parentUuid": "0a0a5b5d_aff699c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "cf4ce0ee0ac0ebc33b6d189a0db0ecf43b012d1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a0a5b5d_dec589a4",
        "filename": "include/console_channel.inc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-20T22:53:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should revise the list and ifdef out channels we can. I bet many of these are added casually when the bit space was ample. It\u0027s easy to extend 32 to 64 but I feel it\u0027s not the right solution.\n\n\u003e radio on nRF51 can be used to implement multiple standards, but only one at a time.\n\nAs long as we do ifdef CONFIG_BLUETOOTH_LE and ifdef CONFIG_ZIGBEE, they won\u0027t occupy extra space, then. If I were debugging bluetooth issue, it would be easier to find channel number because I would be looking for \u0027bluetooth\u0027 in the list of channels dumped by \u0027ch\u0027 command.",
      "parentUuid": "0a0a5b5d_234122f5",
